{#- modules/governance/policy-statement.j2
    A real-looking policy statement, marked up live for the things that make
    it unenforceable.

    Rebuilt from the "Example InfoSec Policy" slide in the 2023 and 2024 "Your
    Governance Is Broken" talks (modules/governance/governance_intro_simple.html,
    reveal.js fragments). Same paragraph, same three categories, same speaker
    beat: read it, agree it sounds fine, then watch it fall apart a colour at
    a time. The original carried a "— ChatGPT" byline; dropped, because the
    point is that this reads like every real policy, not that a model wrote it.

    Three key presses, one category each:
      1. Absolutes      — "all", "every". Nothing is ever all.
      2. Excessive scope — "or", "and", "the company", "mandatory".
      3. Undefined terms — "third-party associates". Who?

    ── Why the highlight is a separate element ─────────────────────
    The engine's `.step` hides with `visibility:hidden`, so putting it on the
    words themselves would make the text vanish and reappear. Instead each
    highlight is an absolutely-positioned rectangle BEHIND the word: the
    sentence is fully readable from the first moment, and only the colour
    arrives on the press. Every rectangle in a category shares a `data-step`
    group so the whole category lands on one press.

    ── Contract note ───────────────────────────────────────────────
    The slide shell uses primitives (`content_slide`, `slide_heading`), but the
    three highlight colours are inline rgba rather than accent names. There is
    no highlight primitive, and the whole point is three distinguishable marks
    on a light document card whose colours must survive a projector. If a
    `highlight` primitive is ever added, this is its first consumer.

    Import WITH CONTEXT:

      {%- from "modules/governance/policy-statement.j2" import
          unenforceable with context %}
-#}

{%- from "modules/branding/" ~ branding ~ "/primitives.j2" import
    content_slide,
    slide_heading
-%}

{%- set RED    = "rgba(239,68,68,0.38)"  -%}
{%- set ORANGE = "rgba(249,115,22,0.38)" -%}
{%- set YELLOW = "rgba(234,179,8,0.42)"  -%}


{%- macro _hl(text, colour, group) -%}
{#- One marked word or phrase. The rectangle is the step; the text is not. -#}
<span style="position:relative; display:inline-block;"><span class="step" data-step="{{ group }}" style="position:absolute; left:-3px; right:-3px; top:-1px; bottom:-1px; background:{{ colour }}; border-radius:3px;"></span><span style="position:relative;">{{ text }}</span></span>
{%- endmacro -%}


{%- macro _legend(colour, group, label) -%}
<span class="step" data-step="{{ group }}" style="display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:8px;">
  <span style="width:16px; height:16px; border-radius:4px; background:{{ colour }};"></span>
  <span>{{ label|safe }}</span>
</span>
{%- endmacro -%}


{%- macro unenforceable() -%}
{%- call content_slide("An example policy") %}
  {{ slide_heading("", "Example Governance") }}

  {#- The document card is deliberately light and serif: it should look like
      the PDF it came from, not like the rest of the deck. -#}
  <div style="background:#f6f5f1; color:#1a1a1a; border-radius:10px; padding:32px 40px; max-width:1000px; margin:8px auto 0; box-shadow:0 8px 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);">
    <p style="font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace; font-size:11px; letter-spacing:0.18em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#6b7280; margin:0 0 14px 0;">Information Security Policy &middot; v3.4</p>
    <p style="font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:19px; line-height:2.0; margin:0 0 16px 0;">
      The scope of this policy extends to {{ _hl("all", RED, "policy-absolute") }} employees, contractors, and
      {{ _hl("third-party associates", YELLOW, "policy-undefined") }} of FinTech Innovations, Inc. who access, process,
      {{ _hl("or", ORANGE, "policy-scope") }} store company data. It applies to {{ _hl("all", RED, "policy-absolute") }}
      forms of data, including electronic and physical formats, and encompasses
      {{ _hl("all", RED, "policy-absolute") }} systems, networks, applications, {{ _hl("and", ORANGE, "policy-scope") }}
      devices managed by {{ _hl("the company", ORANGE, "policy-scope") }}.
    </p>
    <p style="font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:19px; line-height:2.0; margin:0;">
      This policy is integral to our overall risk management strategy and is
      {{ _hl("mandatory", ORANGE, "policy-scope") }} for {{ _hl("all", RED, "policy-absolute") }} personnel to adhere to,
      ensuring that {{ _hl("every", RED, "policy-absolute") }} individual understands their role in safeguarding the
      company&rsquo;s information assets.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div style="display:flex; justify-content:center; gap:36px; margin-top:22px; font-size:15px; color:#94a3b8;">
    {{ _legend(RED,    "policy-absolute",  "<strong>Absolutes</strong> &mdash; nothing is ever <em>all</em>") }}
    {{ _legend(ORANGE, "policy-scope",     "<strong>Excessive scope</strong> &mdash; unbounded by design") }}
    {{ _legend(YELLOW, "policy-undefined", "<strong>Undefined terms</strong> &mdash; who, exactly?") }}
  </div>
{%- endcall %}
{%- endmacro -%}
